WHAT TO PRODUCE (JSON, fields: {{ schema_fields }}):
- `placements` — one row per contents asset (split an asset into 2-3 rows when it appears in
  distinct spots): `count`, `cluster` (x, z), `spread_m`, `faces` (what they look at — a path,
  a doorway, an azimuth), `support` (`ground`, or the asset they stand ON, e.g. bottles on a
  counter).  Put things where the place's activity puts them (stalls line the lane and face it;
  boats lie along the quay edge; a well stands alone) and respect each asset's footprint — two
  clusters closer than the assets are wide will interpenetrate (measured).
- `path_points` — the walkway through this zone as 2-4 (x, z) points, if the description has one.
- `mid_props`, `small_props`, `ground_cover` — how much loose dressing this zone carries beyond
  the placements (the builder invents WHAT they are; you fix HOW MANY; 0 is right for a bare
  place).  The census measures the built zone against these numbers.
- `notes` — one line of intent the builder keeps, e.g. "stalls face the lane, gap at the gate".
